<wpt lat="40.989319599999995" lon="29.0244093">
                  <name>Çiya Sofrası</name>
                  <desc>This place got famous for being featured on an episode of Chef's Table but Turks aren't quite sure what makes it stands out. It is huge and the food is good. They have multiple restaurants all on this one block, I *think* this is the one you're supposed to visit.</desc>
                </wpt>
<wpt lat="40.986745" lon="29.0267737">
                  <name>Kimyon Kadıköy</name>
                  <desc>Classic spot to get all the late-night Turkish food you crave after a night out in the city</desc>
                </wpt>
<wpt lat="40.9866119" lon="29.026559799999998">
                  <name>Karga Bar</name>
                  <desc>Multi-level bar with one? many? performance spaces. We once saw a live-code show here.</desc>
                </wpt>
<wpt lat="40.986596399999996" lon="29.0264904">
                  <name>arkaoda</name>
                  <desc>Chill vibey bar with DJs most nights and experimental music upstairs many nights, check their calendar. Is the original, there's a sister bar in Berlin with the same name.</desc>
                </wpt>
<wpt lat="40.9969356" lon="29.027341999999997">
                  <name>Tarihi Yeldeğirmeni Sokak</name>
                  <desc>Sort of the hipster neighborhood of Istanbul - a lot of coffeeshops and twee stores - ex https://oitheblog.com/2017/02/26/kadikoy-yeldegirmeni-mahallesi-yeni-bir-donusum-hikayesi/</desc>
                </wpt>
